  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\"><em>Digital Disruption</em>, published by Peter Lang Verlag in 2018, shows early traction as a pedagogical anchor and moderate scholarly uptake. The work has accumulated 3 citations across diverse domains\u2014organizational technology, digital learning, and economic transformation\u2014and appears prominently in 5 YouTube-hosted presentations by and featuring the author, alongside institutional library holdings.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Tracey Wilen-Daugenti's <em>Digital Disruption</em> addresses the intersection of technology and organizational change in an era of rapid digital transformation. Published by a peer-reviewed academic press, the work engages with core questions in computer science and technology studies, positioned at the nexus of leadership, information systems, and the social dimensions of technological adoption.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The book demonstrates measurable scholarly uptake through 3 citations recorded in OpenAlex across a four-year period (2019\u20132022). The citing landscape reflects diverse applications: a 2022 chapter on information and communication technology in organizations; a 2021 book on paradigmatic shifts during crisis; and a 2019 contribution on digital learning and organizational obsolescence. These works span management studies and economic development, suggesting the book resonates with scholars examining how institutions navigate technological change.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Beyond traditional citation metrics, the work shows stronger signals of pedagogical adoption and public engagement. Five YouTube presentations\u2014including recorded talks, panels, and broadcast appearances\u2014feature the author and the book's central themes. The work is also catalogued in at least one institutional library, with WorldCat records classifying it under social aspects of technology, leadership, and internet studies. These signals point to active use in teaching contexts and professional development settings.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">At present, the work's scholarly and public impact remains in early stages. With 3 citations and modest institutional holdings, <em>Digital Disruption</em> appears to be establishing a foothold in academic discourse, particularly among scholars working on organizational technology and digital transformation. The concentration of teaching signals around the author's own presentations suggests the book functions as both a research contribution and a resource for knowledge transfer in professional and educational environments.</p>",
